# Optional settings for fridgesheet. Copy to <home>/.env -- ~/.fridgesheet/.env on Linux,
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\fridgesheet\.env on Windows -- which is read automatically; set
# FRIDGESHEET_ENV_FILE only to use a file somewhere else.
# NO CREDENTIALS BELONG IN THIS FILE.
#
# Most of these can also live in <home>/config.toml (README.md, "Settings file"); when both
# set the same thing, the environment wins. The Settings page edits config.toml, not this file.

# Credentials live in the OS credential store (GNOME keyring on Linux, Credential Manager
# on Windows), under service "fridgesheet", keys "username" and "password":
#   fridgesheet set-credentials
# or the Settings page. On Linux they are encrypted at rest under your login password,
# unlocked by PAM at desktop login, and readable by an unattended systemd --user timer.

# Alternative A -- supply them in the environment instead (1Password Environments
# mount, `op run --env-file=...`, or a file you manage yourself). Plaintext at rest:
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_USERNAME=
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_PASSWORD=

# Alternative B -- 1Password CLI secret references, resolved with `op read` at login
# time. Needs someone present to approve the desktop-app prompt, so it is not suitable
# for the timer. Address items by UUID: op:// rejects '(' and ')' in an item title.
# FRIDGESHEET_OP_USERNAME_REF=op://Private/<item-uuid>/username
# FRIDGESHEET_OP_PASSWORD_REF=op://Private/<item-uuid>/password

# --- Only from the process environment (the shell, a unit file, a task) -------------
# These are read before this file is loaded, or by a script that never loads it, so a
# value here has no effect; put them in the environment that starts fridgesheet.
# FRIDGESHEET_HOME=                # the data directory; it decides where this file is looked for
# FRIDGESHEET_ENV_FILE=            # this file's location, if not <home>/.env
# FRIDGESHEET_KEYRING_SERVICE=fridgesheet   # the credential store's service name; read at import
# FRIDGESHEET_COURSE_ALIASES=      # JSON object pairing a class name with the other gradebook's
#                                  # name for it when no rule can, e.g. {"ENGLISH LANGUAGE ARTS": "ELA Plus 5th Gr"}; read at import
# FRIDGESHEET_BIN=                 # scripts/fridgesheet-desktop.sh only: the fridgesheet executable to run

# --- The district ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The defaults are one district's; another district sets all three.
# FRIDGESHEET_CANVAS_BASE=https://lakota.instructure.com
# FRIDGESHEET_HAC_BASE=https://hac.lakotainline.com/HomeAccess
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_HOST=lakota.onelogin.com
# FRIDGESHEET_TIMEZONE=            # IANA name, e.g. America/Chicago; blank = this computer's zone
#                                  # (or [general] timezone in config.toml -- the Settings page's "Where you are")
# FRIDGESHEET_HAC_APP_PATTERN=     # the OneLogin portal tile that opens HAC, found by name
# FRIDGESHEET_HAC_ONELOGIN_APP_URL=   # pin that tile's URL if discovery breaks
# If OneLogin's sign-in form changes (CSS selectors):
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_USER_SELECTOR=
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_PASS_SELECTOR=
# FRIDGESHEET_ONELOGIN_SUBMIT_SELECTOR=

# --- The browser and the pull ------------------------------------------------------
# FRIDGESHEET_HEADLESS=1           # 0 shows the browser window
# FRIDGESHEET_USER_AGENT=          # override the Chrome UA the browser reports (README "Notes")
# FRIDGESHEET_CACHE_TTL_MINUTES=180   # how old a snapshot the MCP tools serve before pulling again

# --- Printing ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRIDGESHEET_PRINTER=             # printer name; blank = system default (`fridgesheet printers` lists them)
# FRIDGESHEET_NICKNAMES=Alex=Al,Katherine=Kate   # snapshot first name = name printed on the sheet
# Also save each PDF here as <school year>/<date> Open Work.pdf (e.g. 2026-27/2026-09-11 Open Work.pdf),
# for a folder people actually look in, such as a Drive mount:
# FRIDGESHEET_SHEETS_ARCHIVE=/path/to/a/folder/people/look/in/Open Work Sheets
# FRIDGESHEET_SUMATRA=             # Windows: SumatraPDF.exe to print with, if not the bundled one

# --- The browser app ---------------------------------------------------------------
# FRIDGESHEET_WEB_HOST=            # bind address; wins over the "Allow other devices" tick.
#                                  # 127.0.0.1 keeps the app off the network; 0.0.0.0 is what the tick does
# FRIDGESHEET_WEB_PORT=8433
# FRIDGESHEET_WEB_NO_BROWSER=1     # the no-argument launcher waits for the server and opens nothing (the smoke test)

# The app's own data-refresh schedule ([refresh]) and each report's schedule ([reports.<key>])
# are config.toml tables, not environment variables -- see the "Settings file" section of
# README.md, or the Schedules page.
